line down
T}
T{
\fB\%k\fR \fB\%\[u2191]\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-p\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-y\fR
T}	T{
line up
T}
T{
\fB\%Space\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-f\fR \fB\%PgDn\fR
T}	T{
page down
T}
T{
\fB\%b\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-b\fR \fB\%Shift\-Space\fR \fB\%PgUp\fR
T}	T{
page up
T}
T{
\fB\%d\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-d\fR / \fB\%u\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-u\fR
T}	T{
half page down / up
T}
T{
\fB\%g\fR \fB\%<\fR \fB\%Home\fR / \fB\%G\fR \fB\%>\fR \fB\%End\fR
T}	T{
top / bottom
T}
T{
\fB\%l\fR
T}	T{
scroll right 8 columns
T}
T{
\fB\%H\fR / \fB\%L\fR
T}	T{
scroll left / right half a screen
T}
T{
\fB\%0\fR / \fB\%$\fR
T}	T{
line start / line end
T}
T{
\fB\%w\fR
T}	T{
toggle wrapped and unwrapped layout
T}
T{
\fB\%f\fR \fB\%t\fR
T}	T{
open the dock with the keyboard in its search field: find in the page
T}
T{
\fB\%/\fR \fB\%o\fR
T}	T{
the same with \fB\%/\fR typed: find a page or project document
T}
T{
\fB\%p\fR
T}	T{
open the dock with the keyboard in its tree, or close it (see Dock)
T}
T{
\fB\%Tab\fR / \fB\%Shift\-Tab\fR
T}	T{
focus next / previous link
T}
T{
\fB\%Enter\fR
T}	T{
follow the focused link (see Links)
T}
T{
\fB\%Backspace\fR \fB\%Alt\-\[u2190]\fR
T}	T{
back to the previous page
T}
T{
\fB\%h\fR
T}	T{
help in place of the page (\fB\%HELP\fR in the title row): the keys as bound and the mouse gestures; \fB\%j\fR/\fB\%k\fR and the other scrolling keys scroll it, \fB\%l\fR, \fB\%H\fR, \fB\%L\fR, \fB\%0\fR, \fB\%$\fR and \fB\%Shift\fR\-wheel sideways, any other key or a click closes it
T}
T{
\fB\%Esc\fR
T}	T{
clear link focus, selection and message
T}
T{
\fB\%Ctrl\-l\fR
T}	T{
redraw
T}
T{
\fB\%q\fR \fB\%Q\fR \fB\%Ctrl\-c\fR
T}	T{
quit
T}
.TE
.PP
Bindings are looked up by physical key first (the kitty base\-layout code), then by the reported key, then by the shifted symbol without its shift. That makes \fB\%G\fR and \fB\%$\fR work on any layout.
.PP
The status row shows messages such as \fB\%Copied \%29 \%characters\fR on the left. On the right it shows the layout, the visible lines of the body and the first column: \fB\%[wrap] \%\[u2502] \%1\-56/801 \%\[u2502] \%col \%1\fR. While finding in the page it starts with the selected match and the match count, during a \fB\%/\fR search with the result count; then the progress of indexing (\fB\%indexing \%40%\fR, while page descriptions load) and of reading the text of all pages (\fB\%reading \%pages \%40%\fR). While the help is shown it shows the help\(aqs visible lines and first column instead of the page\(aqs.
.SS
Dock
.PP
The dock sits left of the page: the search field between \fB\%\[u25D6]\fR and \fB\%\[u25D7]\fR on its first row (\fB\%find\fR while empty), then the tree of pages, with a divider on its right edge that joins the lines above and below (\fB\%\[u252C]\fR, \fB\%\[u2534]\fR). \fB\%p\fR opens it with the keyboard in the tree and closes it; \fB\%f\fR, \fB\%t\fR or a click on the field opens it with the keyboard in the field, \fB\%/\fR and \fB\%o\fR with \fB\%/\fR already typed. A regular dock narrows the page; an overlay dock (\fB\%dock \%= \%overlay\fR) covers the left of the page on the popup background. Dragging the divider resizes it. Keys the tree does not bind go to the page, so \fB\%Space\fR, \fB\%b\fR, \fB\%d\fR and \fB\%u\fR scroll the page with the keyboard in the tree.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBThe tree\fR shows the pages around the current one: for a page of the project, or without a page, the project\(aqs pages (\fB\%name(section)\fR) and Markdown documents (by their path from the project root: \fB\%README.md\fR, \fB\%docs/guide.md\fR); for another page, the outermost group it is in (all of \fB\%abrt\fR for \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops(1)\fR), or the page alone when it is in none. Names that share a prefix fold into nested groups: \fB\%abrt\-cli\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR go under \fB\%\[u25B8] \%abrt\fR, and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-xorg\fR under \fB\%\[u25B8] \%abrt\-dump\fR within it. A prefix is made of whole tokens of the name, split at \fB\%\-\fR, \fB\%_\fR, \fB\%.\fR, \fB\%:\fR and \fB\%/\fR (so \fB\%File::Spec\fR, \fB\%systemd.unit\fR and the project\(aqs \fB\%docs/guide.md\fR group too), and it takes at least 3 entries to make a group. Groups cross sections (\fB\%abrt(1)\fR, \fB\%abrt.conf(5)\fR) and are case\-sensitive; a page named like its group (\fB\%git(1)\fR in \fB\%git\fR) is listed inside it. Rows are named relative to their group, so \fB\%abrt\-action\-analyze\-c(1)\fR reads \fB\%c(1)\fR under \fB\%\[u25BE] \%analyze\fR under \fB\%\[u25BE] \%action\fR under \fB\%\[u25BE] \%abrt\fR; a page named like its group is named relative to the group above (\fB\%abrt(1)\fR in \fB\%abrt\fR, \fB\%dump(1)\fR in \fB\%abrt\-dump\fR). The groups are folded and listed by name, except those around the current page, which is selected; the tree follows the page through links, \fB\%Backspace\fR and pages opened from the tree, switching to the group of a page in another one.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBText without a leading \fB\%/\fB\fR fuzzy\-finds in the lines of the displayed page, in its current layout. The page stays in the frame: matched characters are highlighted where they are, the selected match\(aqs line is shaded, and the page scrolls to the best match as you type. \fB\%\[u2193]\fR/\fB\%\[u2191]\fR step through the matches, best first, and the status row shows \fB\%match \%2/8\fR. \fB\%Enter\fR gives the page the keyboard at the match. Meanwhile the lines that every term matches are counted for every page of the manual, and the tree shows each of its pages\(aq count at the right of the row with the name in the \fB\%hit\fR color; a group shows how many of its pages have hits. The text of all pages is read once, in the background, by worker processes (\fB\%search\-threads\fR, \fB\%docv \%text\-worker\fR), with progress in the status row, and cached in \fB\%$XDG_CACHE_HOME/docv/text.bin\fR (about 200 MB for 27,000 pages) with each page\(aqs modification time; later sessions read only changed pages. Searching it takes threads of their own, tens of milliseconds for a full manual. Fuzzy terms are lenient, so short ones match a line of most pages.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBText after a leading \fB\%/\fB\fR fills the tree with every page along the manual path and every document of the project, the project\(aqs first, and ranks them, each row with its description (from the NAME section; for a document its first heading and paragraph) after the name. A term matches the reference or the description and counts with the better of the two; a reference match counts half a character more than an equal description match. So \fB\%/printf \%3\fR finds \fB\%printf(3)\fR, and \fB\%/list \%dir\fR finds \fB\%dir(1)\fR and \fB\%ls(1)\fR by their descriptions. The project\(aqs entries still come first, ahead of better matches elsewhere; ties go to the shorter reference, then to section order. Groups without a match are left out and the others are open and ranked by their best match, each level on its own; folding one keeps it folded until the text changes. \fB\%Enter\fR (in the field or the tree) or a click opens the selected page or document and ends the search: the field empties, the tree shows the page\(aqs group and the page gets the keyboard; \fB\%Backspace\fR in the page view comes back. Without a page on the command line the viewer starts here.
.PP
Both are fuzzy: the characters of each space\-separated term must appear in order, and matches score higher at word starts, in runs of consecutive characters and with short gaps (scored like fzf). Every term must match. Lower\-case terms ignore case; a term with an upper\-case letter matches exactly. Matched characters are underlined in the results. Rows wider than the dock scroll sideways.
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
