T}
T{
\fB\%Enter\fR
T}	T{
open the page / fold or unfold the group
T}
T{
\fB\%l\fR \fB\%\[u2192]\fR / \fB\%\[u2190]\fR
T}	T{
unfold the group or step into it / fold it or step out to its group
T}
T{
\fB\%L\fR \fB\%Shift\-\[u2192]\fR / \fB\%H\fR \fB\%Shift\-\[u2190]\fR
T}	T{
scroll the tree right / left
T}
T{
\fB\%Tab\fR
T}	T{
to the search field
T}
T{
\fB\%Esc\fR
T}	T{
back to the page
T}
.TE
.PP
Page names are listed on the spot. Descriptions come from parsing the start of each page, which takes a few seconds for a full manual. That work runs in the background while the dock is open, with progress shown in the status row; the project\(aqs documents are described first. The page descriptions are cached in \fB\%$XDG_CACHE_HOME/docv/index.tsv\fR (\fB\%\(ti/.cache/docv/index.tsv\fR when the variable is unset or not absolute). A directory whose modification time is unchanged comes from the cache; in a changed directory only files with a new modification time are read again. Document descriptions are read on every start. Quitting early keeps the descriptions done so far.
.SS
Links
.PP
\fB\%Tab\fR focuses the links on the page in turn, the status row shows where the focused one leads, and \fB\%Enter\fR or a click follows it. \fB\%Backspace\fR comes back to the place it was followed from.
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBLink\fR
T}	T{
\fBFollowing it\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%name(section)\fR in the text
T}	T{
opens the page from the search path
T}
T{
\fB\%[text](other.md#usage)\fR
T}	T{
opens the file relative to the current one, at the heading \fB\%usage\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%[text](#usage)\fR
T}	T{
goes to the heading \fB\%usage\fR of the current document
T}
T{
\fB\%[text](https://\[u2026])\fR, \fB\%mailto:\fR \[u2026]
T}	T{
shows the URL; the terminal opens it (OSC 8)
T}
.TE
.PP
Anchors are GitHub\(aqs: the heading in lower case, punctuation dropped, spaces as dashes, \fB\%\-1\fR, \fB\%\-2\fR\[u2026] appended to repeated headings. Links with a scheme are written to the terminal as OSC 8 hyperlinks. Most terminals open them on a click with a modifier (kitty: \fB\%Ctrl\-Shift\fR\-click), because the viewer takes plain clicks itself.
.SS
Mouse
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
