T}
.TE
.PP
A selection stays highlighted until the next click or key. Selections follow the indentation: a line\(aqs indentation and trailing blanks are never highlighted, and the copied lines lose the indentation they share, so a paragraph comes out flush left and code keeps its relative indentation.
.PP
The arrow keys \fB\%\[u2190]\fR and \fB\%\[u2192]\fR do not scroll sideways; \fB\%l\fR, \fB\%H\fR, \fB\%L\fR, \fB\%0\fR, \fB\%$\fR, \fB\%Shift\fR\-wheel and the horizontal scrollbar do. Code never wraps, also in the wrapped layout: code blocks (\fB\%.EX\fR, \fB\%.nf\fR, \fB\%.Bd \%\-literal\fR, \fB\%.Dl\fR, fenced and indented Markdown code) keep their lines, and Markdown code spans are not broken across lines; the page scrolls sideways to show long ones. The clipboard write first sends an invalid payload, which clears the clipboard in terminals that append successive OSC 52 writes (kitty) and is ignored elsewhere.
.SH
MARKDOWN
.PP
Markdown is read as CommonMark with the GitHub extensions: tables, task lists, strikethrough, bare URLs as links (\fB\%www.\fR, \fB\%https://\fR, e\-mail addresses) and alerts (\fB\%> \%[!NOTE]\fR).
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBElement\fR
T}	T{
\fBShown as\fR
T}
_
T{
paragraph
T}	T{
filled to the width; a hard line break (two spaces, \fB\%\e\fR) starts a new line
T}
T{
heading \fB\%#\fR \[u2026] \fB\%######\fR
T}	T{
its own line in the role of its level (\fB\%heading1\fR \[u2026] \fB\%heading6\fR), with a blank line after
T}
T{
\fB\%**bold**\fR, \fB\%*italic*\fR
T}	T{
the \fB\%bold\fR and \fB\%italic\fR roles
T}
T{
\fB\%\(ti\(tistrikethrough\(ti\(ti\fR
T}	T{
struck through (SGR 9)
T}
T{
\fB\%\(gacode\(ga\fR
T}	T{
the \fB\%code\fR role
T}
T{
code block
T}	T{
its lines unwrapped, indented by 4, in \fB\%code\-block\fR; tabs every 8 columns
T}
T{
list
T}	T{
items hanging on \fB\%\[u2022]\fR \fB\%\[u25E6]\fR \fB\%\[u25AA]\fR by depth, \fB\%1.\fR (widest number), \fB\%\[u2610]\fR / \fB\%\[u2611]\fR for tasks; loose lists keep a blank line between items
T}
T{
block quote
T}	T{
a \fB\%\[u2502]\fR bar per level, in \fB\%quote\fR; an alert starts with its title (\fB\%Note\fR) in bold
T}
T{
table
T}	T{
boxed as wide as the terminal (spare width spread over the columns by their widths), the header row bold and ruled off, cells aligned and filled to their column
T}
T{
\fB\%\-\-\-\fR
T}	T{
a rule across the width, in \fB\%rule\fR
T}
T{
image
T}	T{
its description, in \fB\%image\fR (the file name without one)
T}
T{
raw HTML
T}	T{
dropped, keeping the text between the tags
T}
.TE
.PP
Markdown documents have no page header and footer; the title row shows the file name and first heading.
.SH
SYNTAX HIGHLIGHTING
.PP
With \fB\%syntax\-highlighting \%= \%true\fR (the default), code examples are colored by their syntax through tree\-sitter:
.IP \(bu 2
Markdown code blocks labeled with a language: \fB\%\(ga\(ga\(gacrystal\fR. The first word of the label names the grammar, or an alias of it (\fB\%cr\fR \[u2192] \fB\%crystal\fR, \fB\%sh\fR/\fB\%shell\fR \[u2192] \fB\%bash\fR, \fB\%js\fR \[u2192] \fB\%javascript\fR, \fB\%py\fR \[u2192] \fB\%python\fR, \fB\%yml\fR \[u2192] \fB\%yaml\fR, \[u2026]). Unlabeled and indented code blocks and code spans stay plain.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fB\%.EX\fR examples of manual pages whose section names a language: \fB\%Foo.3cr\fR and \fB\%name.7cr\fR, the pages \fB\%docv \%gen\-cr\fR makes, are Crystal.
.PP
A language takes two things, and docv ships neither: its grammar, a shared library \fB\%libtree\-sitter\-<name>.so\fR or \fB\%<name>.so\fR, and its highlight query, \fB\%<name>/highlights.scm\fR. They are looked for where tree\-sitter and editors install them, for example grammars in \fB\%\(ti/.local/lib\fR with queries in \fB\%\(ti/.local/share/tree\-sitter/queries/<name>/highlights.scm\fR:
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBGrammars (after \fB\%\(ti/.local/lib\fB, \fB\%/usr/local/lib\fB, \fB\%/usr/local/lib64\fB, \fB\%/usr/lib\fB, \fB\%/usr/lib64\fB)\fR
T}	T{
\fBQueries\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/docv/grammars\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/docv/queries\fR, \fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/tree\-sitter/queries\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/nvim/site/parser\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/nvim/site/queries\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/nvim/lazy/nvim\-treesitter/parser\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/nvim/lazy/nvim\-treesitter/queries\fR, \fB\%/usr/share/nvim/runtime/queries\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/helix/runtime/grammars\fR, \fB\%/usr/lib64\fR, \fB\%/usr/lib\fR and \fB\%/usr/share\fR \fB\%helix/runtime/grammars\fR
T}	T{
the same \fB\%helix/runtime/queries\fR directories
T}
.TE
.PP
(\fB\%XDG_DATA_HOME\fR defaults to \fB\%\(ti/.local/share\fR, \fB\%XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR to \fB\%\(ti/.config\fR.) A grammar can be built from its repository with \fB\%tree\-sitter \%build\fR, whose \fB\%queries/highlights.scm\fR is the query. A query\(aqs \fB\%; \%inherits: \%a,b\fR line puts those languages\(aq queries first. A language without a grammar or query, or whose query the grammar rejects, stays plain.
.PP
Capture names map to the \fB\%syntax\-*\fR roles by their longest known dotted prefix (\fB\%keyword.function\fR is a keyword; nvim\(aqs and helix\(aqs names both work); \fB\%variable\fR and unknown names stay in the code\(aqs own color (\fB\%code\-block\fR in documents, plain in manual pages). An inner capture overrides the one around it. Of two captures of the same node, the later pattern wins, as in nvim; for helix\(aqs query directories the earlier one does.
.SH
LIBRARY
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
require "docv"

doc = Docv.open("ls", "1") || abort "no page"   # find + load (added directories and system path)
manpath = Docv::Manpath.default(Dir.current)    # with the man pages of the project around the current directory
path = manpath.find("tool", "1")
doc = Docv.load("/usr/share/man/man1/ls.1.gz")  # file, plain or gzip
doc = Docv.load("README.md")                    # Markdown by file name (Markdown.file?)
doc = Docv.parse(source, path)                  # roff text; path resolves .so
doc = Docv::Markdown.parse(text)                # Markdown text
doc = Docv.load(path, Docv::Options.new(unsafe: true, stdin: STDIN))
doc = Docv.load(path, Docv::Config.load.options) # options from config.ini
doc = Docv.load("README.md", Docv::Options.new(highlight: true))  # with syntax highlighting

doc.format     # Docv::Format::Man | Mdoc | Roff | Markdown
doc.reference  # "LS(1)"; a document\(aqs first level 1 heading
doc.title, doc.section, doc.date, doc.source, doc.manual
doc.blocks     # Array(Docv::Block)
doc.links      # Array(Docv::Target): the targets of Span#link (from 1)
doc.anchors    # heading anchor => block index ("installation" => 12)
doc.messages   # .tm output and unknown requests or macros

Docv::Layout.new(doc).header_line(80)          # the page header line, nil without .TH/.Dt and for Markdown
Docv::Layout.new(doc).footer_line(80)          # the page footer line, nil without .TH/.Dt and for Markdown
Docv::Layout.new(doc).lines(80, header: false, footer: false)  # the body only
Docv::Layout.new(doc).lines(80, wrap: true).each do |line|
  puts line.text                       # cells as text
  line.links.each { |link| p link }    # Layout::Link: col, width, target (Target: kind, location, part)
end

index = Docv::Index.new(manpath)        # pages along the manpath and its project\(aqs documents
index.describe unless index.complete?      # parse the descriptions still missing; saves the cache
index.entries.each { |entry| puts "#{entry.reference}  #{entry.description}" }
Docv::Index.description(path)           # one page\(aqs NAME description, one document\(aqs heading and paragraph

project = Docv::Manpath.project(Dir.current)  # root, man page directories, Markdown documents

fuzzy = Docv::Fuzzy.new("prf")
fuzzy.score("printf")                      # => 73 (nil when not a subsequence)
fuzzy.positions("printf")                  # => [0, 1, 5]
.EE
.RE
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBType\fR
T}	T{
\fBHolds\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%Document\fR
T}	T{
metadata, blocks, link targets (\fB\%links\fR) and heading anchors (\fB\%anchors\fR) of a page or document
T}
T{
\fB\%Block\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%kind\fR (\fB\%Text\fR, \fB\%Heading\fR, \fB\%Blank\fR, \fB\%Table\fR, \fB\%Rule\fR), heading \fB\%level\fR (1\-6), \fB\%indent\fR, first\-line \fB\%offset\fR, \fB\%tag\fR/\fB\%tag_indent\fR, \fB\%fill?\fR, \fB\%align\fR, \fB\%tabs\fR, \fB\%spans\fR, \fB\%lines\fR, \fB\%table\fR, quote \fB\%bars\fR (columns)
T}
T{
\fB\%Span\fR
T}	T{
text, a style id (\fB\%Styles[id]\fR is a \fB\%Style\fR: \fB\%attr\fR (\fB\%Attr\fR: \fB\%Bold\fR, \fB\%Italic\fR, \fB\%Underline\fR, \fB\%Reverse\fR, \fB\%Dim\fR, \fB\%Strike\fR), \fB\%fg\fR, \fB\%bg\fR, \fB\%markup\fR; \fB\%merge(over)\fR) and a \fB\%link\fR (index into \fB\%Document#links\fR from 1, \fB\%0\fR for none)
T}
T{
\fB\%Markup\fR
T}	T{
what text is for the viewer\(aqs roles: \fB\%None\fR, \fB\%Code\fR, \fB\%CodeBlock\fR, \fB\%Quote\fR, \fB\%Rule\fR, \fB\%Image\fR, and \fB\%SyntaxKeyword\fR \[u2026] \fB\%SyntaxTag\fR for highlighted code
T}
T{
\fB\%Target\fR
T}	T{
where a link leads: \fB\%kind\fR (\fB\%TargetKind\fR: \fB\%Page\fR, \fB\%Url\fR, \fB\%File\fR, \fB\%Anchor\fR), \fB\%location\fR (page name, URL, path), \fB\%part\fR (section, anchor), \fB\%label\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Syntax\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Syntax.highlight(code, \%language)\fR (lines of \fB\%{text, \%Markup}\fR runs, \fB\%nil\fR without grammar or query), \fB\%apply(blocks, \%language)\fR, \fB\%language(label)\fR (\fB\%ALIASES\fR), \fB\%page_language(path)\fR (\fB\%SECTION_LANGUAGES\fR), \fB\%markup(capture)\fR (\fB\%CAPTURES\fR), \fB\%grammar_directories\fR, \fB\%query_directories\fR (\fB\%Syntax::QueryDirectory\fR: \fB\%path\fR, \fB\%first_wins\fR), \fB\%clear\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Markdown\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Markdown.parse(text, \%highlight \%= \%false)\fR, \fB\%Markdown.file?(path)\fR (\fB\%EXTENSIONS\fR), \fB\%Markdown.slug(heading)\fR, \fB\%Markdown.description(text)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Color\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Color::DEFAULT\fR, \fB\%Color.palette(index)\fR (0\-255), \fB\%Color.rgb(r, \%g, \%b)\fR; \fB\%default?\fR, \fB\%palette?\fR, \fB\%rgb?\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Palette\fR
T}	T{
the terminal theme as RGB: \fB\%foreground\fR, \fB\%background\fR, \fB\%set(key, \%value)\fR (OSC 21 values), \fB\%reported?\fR, \fB\%dark?\fR, \fB\%rgb(color, \%foreground)\fR, \fB\%ramp(rgb, \%percent)\fR, \fB\%reduce(color, \%depth)\fR; \fB\%Palette.parse(value)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Theme\fR
T}	T{
role styles: \fB\%Theme.new(overrides)\fR, \fB\%Theme.parse(spec)\fR, \fB\%styles(palette, \%depth)\fR (a style id per \fB\%Theme::Role\fR), \fB\%Theme::DEFAULT\fR, \fB\%Theme::MONOCHROME\fR, \fB\%Theme::KEYS\fR; \fB\%Theme::Error\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Table\fR
T}	T{
tbl rows of cells (\fB\%Text\fR, \fB\%HSpan\fR, \fB\%VSpan\fR, \fB\%Rule\fR, \fB\%DoubleRule\fR), alignments, minimum widths, vertical rules, gaps, frame
T}
T{
\fB\%Layout::Line\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%cells \%: \%Array(Cell)\fR, \fB\%text\fR, \fB\%links\fR, \fB\%block\fR/\fB\%offset\fR (reading position)
T}
T{
\fB\%Cell\fR
T}	T{
grapheme, style id, width (2 for wide characters, 0 for their continuation)
T}
T{
\fB\%Manpath\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Manpath.new(dirs, \%locale, \%project \%= \%nil)\fR (each dir a tree or a flat directory), \fB\%find(name, \%section)\fR, \fB\%roots\fR (\fB\%Manpath::Root\fR: \fB\%path\fR, \fB\%flat\fR, \fB\%project\fR), \fB\%project\fR, \fB\%all_sections\fR; \fB\%Manpath.default(dir \%= \%nil)\fR (project directories, added directories, system path, with the project around \fIdir\fR), \fB\%Manpath.system(manpath, \%path, \%config)\fR, \fB\%Manpath.man_db\fR/\fB\%parse_man_db\fR, \fB\%Manpath.project_root(dir)\fR, \fB\%Manpath.project(dir)\fR (\fB\%Manpath::Project\fR: \fB\%root\fR, \fB\%pages\fR, \fB\%documents\fR), \fB\%Manpath.discover(dir)\fR, \fB\%Manpath.flat?\fR/\fB\%pages?\fR/\fB\%page?\fR, \fB\%Manpath.split(file, \%section)\fR, \fB\%Manpath.read_paths\fR/\fB\%add_paths\fR/\fB\%remove_paths\fR/\fB\%paths_file\fR, \fB\%Manpath.parse_reference\fR, \fB\%Manpath.rank(section)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Index\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Index.new(manpath \%= \%Manpath.default, \%cache \%= \%Index.cache_path)\fR (\fB\%nil\fR cache disables it), \fB\%entries\fR (the project\(aqs pages, its documents, the other pages), \fB\%pending\fR, \fB\%complete?\fR, \fB\%describe\fR (optionally with a block receiving done and total after each entry; \fB\%break\fR stops early), \fB\%save\fR, \fB\%Index.description(path)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Index::Entry\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%name\fR (a document\(aqs path from the project root), \fB\%section\fR (empty for a document), \fB\%path\fR, \fB\%description\fR, \fB\%reference\fR, \fB\%project?\fR, \fB\%document?\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Fuzzy\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Fuzzy.new(query)\fR, \fB\%score(text)\fR, \fB\%positions(text)\fR (character indices), \fB\%exact?\fR (query has upper case)
T}
T{
\fB\%Source\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Source.read(path)\fR: gzip inflating and Latin\-1 fallback; \fB\%.so\fR resolution
T}
T{
\fB\%Options\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%unsafe\fR (run \fB\%Roff::Engine::UNSAFE\fR requests and \fB\%\eV\fR), \fB\%stdin\fR (input of \fB\%.rd\fR; \fB\%nil\fR reads nothing), \fB\%highlight\fR (syntax highlighting, default \fB\%false\fR; \fB\%Config#options\fR sets it from \fB\%syntax\-highlighting\fR)
T}
T{
\fB\%Config\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Config.load(path \%= \%Config.path, \%create \%= \%true)\fR, \fB\%Config.parse(text)\fR, \fB\%unsafe?\fR, \fB\%start_wrapped?\fR, \fB\%syntax_highlighting?\fR, \fB\%colors\fR, \fB\%theme\fR, \fB\%options(stdin)\fR, \fB\%viewer\fR (\fB\%ViewerSettings\fR: \fB\%dock\fR (\fB\%DockStyle::Regular\fR, \fB\%Overlay\fR), \fB\%dock_width\fR, \fB\%dock_open\fR, \fB\%search_threads\fR); \fB\%Config::Error\fR
T}
.TE
.PP
The man page generator is a separate require too:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
require "docv/crystal_pages"

root = Docv::CrystalPages::Shard.root(Dir.current) || abort "not in a shard"
puts Docv::CrystalPages.generate(root, File.join(root, "man"))  # "man: 12 written, 3 unchanged, 0 removed"
.EE
.RE
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBType\fR
T}	T{
\fBDoes\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%generate(root, \%output)\fR, \fB\%blocks(markdown)\fR (markd nodes), \fB\%summary\fR, \fB\%base_name\fR, \fB\%clean_type\fR, \fB\%plain\fR; \fB\%GENERATOR\fR, \fB\%MARKER\fR, \fB\%GENERATED\fR, \fB\%SUFFIX\fR; \fB\%CrystalPages::Error\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::DocTool\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%load(root)\fR: runs \fB\%crystal \%docs \%\-\-format \%json\fR into a \fB\%Project\fR (\fB\%repository_name\fR, \fB\%body\fR, \fB\%program\fR)
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::TypeDoc\fR
T}	T{
a documented type: kind, names, superclass and relations, constants, constructors, methods, macros, nested types (generated members dropped)
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::Shard\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Shard.root(dir)\fR, \fB\%name\fR, \fB\%version\fR, \fB\%require_path(type)\fR, \fB\%relative(text)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::Types\fR
T}	T{
the types with pages, \fB\%[]?(name)\fR, \fB\%lookup(context, \%name)\fR, \fB\%referenced(type)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::Renderer\fR
T}	T{
markd blocks to roff: \fB\%render(blocks)\fR, \fB\%item(head, \%blocks)\fR, \fB\%tables?\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::Inline\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%render(node, \%bold:, \%urls:, \%upcase:)\fR, \fB\%markdown(text, \%urls:)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::Pages\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%all\fR: the overview and type \fB\%Page\fRs (\fB\%path\fR, \fB\%name\fR, \fB\%section\fR, \fB\%body\fR, \fB\%render(date)\fR)
T}
T{
\fB\%CrystalPages::Generator\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%run(pages)\fR: written, unchanged, removed; \fB\%Generator.today\fR (\fB\%SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH\fR)
T}
.TE
.PP
The viewer and its terminal layer are a separate require:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
require "docv/viewer"

config = Docv::Config.load
viewer = Docv::Viewer.new(doc, path, wrap: true, options: config.options, theme: config.theme,
  settings: config.viewer)
viewer.bindings[{Docv::Term::Mods::None, \(aqx\(aq.ord}] = Docv::Viewer::Action::Quit
viewer.field_bindings[{Docv::Term::Mods::Ctrl, \(aqj\(aq.ord}] = Docv::Viewer::FieldAction::Next
viewer.run

start = Docv::Viewer.new                        # empty page, dock closed
start.perform(Docv::Viewer::Action::OpenPage)   # start in a search of every page
start.run
.EE
.RE
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBType\fR
T}	T{
\fBDoes\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%Viewer\fR
T}	T{
the full\-screen viewer; \fB\%run\fR, \fB\%perform(action)\fR, \fB\%bindings\fR, \fB\%field_bindings\fR, \fB\%tree_bindings\fR, \fB\%focus\fR (\fB\%Page\fR, \fB\%Tree\fR, \fB\%Field\fR); the document is optional (empty page); \fB\%options\fR apply to pages opened through links and the page search (\fB\%.rd\fR never reads there); \fB\%theme\fR (default \fB\%Theme.new\fR), \fB\%depth\fR (default \fB\%Term::Tty.color_depth\fR) and \fB\%settings\fR (\fB\%ViewerSettings\fR: \fB\%dock\fR style, \fB\%dock_width\fR, \fB\%dock_open\fR, \fB\%search_threads\fR; \fB\%Config#viewer\fR)
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Keymap(T)\fR
T}	T{
key table, \fB\%lookup(event)\fR with physical/key/shifted matching
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Bindings\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Keymap(Action)\fR for the page view, from \fB\%DEFAULT_BINDINGS\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::FieldBindings\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Keymap(FieldAction)\fR for the search field, from \fB\%FIELD_BINDINGS\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::TreeBindings\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%Keymap(TreeAction)\fR for the dock\(aqs tree, from \fB\%TREE_BINDINGS\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Picker\fR
T}	T{
fuzzy\-ranked list of \fB\%Item\fRs (label, detail, target, role, group; lower groups first; key): \fB\%query=\fR, \fB\%results\fR, \fB\%rows\fR, \fB\%current\fR, \fB\%group?\fR, \fB\%toggle\fR, \fB\%expand\fR, \fB\%collapse\fR, \fB\%reveal(target)\fR, \fB\%move\fR, \fB\%scroll_to\fR, \fB\%scroll_x\fR/\fB\%left\fR/\fB\%width\fR (sideways), \fB\%hits=\fR (counts per item, groups count items with hits), \fB\%marks\fR, \fB\%label_width\fR, \fB\%draw\fR (with the role style ids, a fill, labels only without details); \fB\%nested: \%true\fR folds the items into an \fB\%Outline\fR by their keys
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Picker::Outline\fR
T}	T{
items grouped by shared key prefixes (\fB\%SEPARATORS\fR, \fB\%MIN_GROUP\fR): \fB\%nodes\fR (\fB\%Node\fR: prefix, item, parent, depth, size, children, text and skip of the relative name), \fB\%roots\fR, \fB\%leaf\fR, \fB\%items(id)\fR, \fB\%Outline.each_token\fR, \fB\%Outline.relative\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Dock\fR
T}	T{
the dock: \fB\%field\fR, \fB\%group\fR and \fB\%pages\fR (nested \fB\%Picker\fRs: the current page\(aqs group, every page), \fB\%tree\fR (the one shown), \fB\%style\fR, \fB\%width\fR, \fB\%open?\fR, \fB\%span(cols)\fR, \fB\%offset(cols)\fR, \fB\%manual?\fR, \fB\%query\fR, \fB\%part(frame, \%row, \%col)\fR (\fB\%Field\fR, \fB\%Rule\fR, \fB\%Tree\fR, \fB\%Divider\fR), \fB\%tree_row\fR, \fB\%tree_rows\fR, \fB\%tree_cols\fR, \fB\%draw\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Frame\fR
T}	T{
title row with name, page heading and close mark, title line, content area (after a regular dock\(aqs columns, \fB\%dock\fR) with the scrollbars, status row: geometry (\fB\%inner\fR, \fB\%left\fR, \fB\%inner_cols\fR, \fB\%content_cols\fR), \fB\%name_width\fR, \fB\%heading_bounds\fR, \fB\%heading_col(width)\fR, \fB\%region(row, \%col)\fR (\fB\%Name\fR, \fB\%Title\fR, \fB\%Close\fR, \fB\%Border\fR, \fB\%Content\fR, \fB\%VerticalBar\fR, \fB\%HorizontalBar\fR, \fB\%Status\fR), \fB\%Frame.thumb\fR, \fB\%draw\fR, \fB\%title\fR, \fB\%rule\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Help\fR
T}	T{
the help from the bindings, drawn in the page area (\fB\%Help::TITLE\fR heads the title row) (\fB\%ACTION_HELP\fR, \fB\%FIELD_HELP\fR, \fB\%TREE_HELP\fR, \fB\%Help::MOUSE\fR): \fB\%lines\fR, \fB\%top\fR, \fB\%left\fR, \fB\%width\fR, \fB\%keys_width\fR, \fB\%scroll\fR, \fB\%scroll_x\fR, \fB\%rows\fR, \fB\%max_top\fR, \fB\%max_left\fR, \fB\%draw\fR, \fB\%Help.key_name(mods, \%key)\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Viewer::Field\fR
T}	T{
the search field text: \fB\%insert\fR, \fB\%delete_back\fR, \fB\%clear\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Corpus\fR
T}	T{
the text of many pages (\fB\%require \%"docv/corpus"\fR): \fB\%build(sources)\fR from its mapped cache file (\fB\%text.bin\fR) or by parsing, in \fB\%threads\fR worker processes when \fB\%Corpus.worker\fR is set (\fB\%Corpus.serve\fR, \fB\%docv \%text\-worker\fR); \fB\%text(index)\fR, \fB\%count(query, \%cancelled)\fR (lines every term matches per page, on isolated searcher threads), \fB\%Corpus.extract(path)\fR, \fB\%close\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%Screen\fR
T}	T{
front and back cell buffers with hyperlinks; \fB\%write\fR, \fB\%blit\fR, \fB\%fill\fR, \fB\%restyle\fR, \fB\%link(row, \%col, \%count, \%uri)\fR (OSC 8), \fB\%colors(palette, \%depth)\fR, \fB\%render(io)\fR rewrites changed rows only, with colors reduced to the depth
T}
T{
\fB\%Term::Tty\fR
T}	T{
raw mode, window size in cells and pixels, \fB\%enter\fR/\fB\%leave\fR of the full\-screen state, \fB\%query_colors\fR (OSC 21), \fB\%copy(text)\fR (OSC 52 clipboard), \fB\%pointer(shape)\fR (OSC 22), \fB\%Tty.color_depth\fR (\fB\%NO_COLOR\fR, \fB\%COLORTERM\fR, \fB\%TERM\fR)
T}
T{
\fB\%Term::Decoder\fR
T}	T{
bytes into raw events: \fB\%KeyEvent\fR, \fB\%MouseEvent\fR, \fB\%ResizeEvent\fR, \fB\%FocusEvent\fR, \fB\%VisibilityEvent\fR, \fB\%ColorSchemeEvent\fR, \fB\%ModeReport\fR, \fB\%CellSizeReport\fR, \fB\%KeyboardFlagsReport\fR, \fB\%ColorsReport\fR (OSC 21)
T}
T{
\fB\%Term::Input\fR
T}	T{
derived events: pressed\-set, \fB\%TextInput\fR/\fB\%KeyCommand\fR, \fB\%MousePress\fR, \fB\%Click\fR (with multi\-click count), \fB\%Drag\fR (start/move/end), \fB\%Scroll\fR (accumulated), \fB\%PointerEnter\fR/\fB\%PointerMove\fR/\fB\%PointerLeave\fR; pixel\-to\-cell conversion
T}
.TE
.SS
Terminal modes
.PP
On entering, the viewer switches to the alternate screen and pushes kitty keyboard flags \fB\%31\fR inside it (\fB\%CSI \%> \%31 \%u\fR). It enables mouse modes 1003, 1006 and 1016 and notification modes 2048, 1004, 2033 and 2031, then queries mode 1016, the cell size, the keyboard flags, visibility and the color scheme, and the theme colors with OSC 21 (again when the color scheme changes). On leaving it undoes all of this in reverse order. Mouse coordinates are read as pixels once the terminal confirms mode 1016; otherwise they are read as SGR cell coordinates. Frames are written inside synchronized\-update brackets (mode 2026). URL links are written as OSC 8 hyperlinks, ended before the end of each row. The mouse pointer is shaped with OSC 22 (kitty\(aqs pointer shapes, CSS cursor names) after each frame when what lies under it changed: \fB\%text\fR over page text and the search field, \fB\%pointer\fR over links, rows of the tree and the close mark, \fB\%ew\-resize\fR over the dock\(aqs edge, \fB\%grab\fR over a scrollbar thumb and \fB\%grabbing\fR while dragging one, \fB\%default\fR elsewhere; leaving resets it.
.SH
ROFF COVERAGE
.PP
Every groff request is recognized.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInterpreted:\fR definitions and strings (\fB\%de\fR \fB\%am\fR \fB\%ds\fR \fB\%as\fR and their \fB\%1\fR/\fB\%i\fR variants, \fB\%rm\fR \fB\%rn\fR \fB\%als\fR \fB\%chop\fR \fB\%length\fR \fB\%substring\fR \fB\%stringup\fR \fB\%stringdown\fR); registers (\fB\%nr\fR \fB\%rr\fR \fB\%rnn\fR \fB\%aln\fR \fB\%af\fR); conditionals and loops (\fB\%if\fR \fB\%ie\fR \fB\%el\fR \fB\%while\fR \fB\%break\fR \fB\%continue\fR); \fB\%return\fR \fB\%shift\fR \fB\%nop\fR \fB\%do\fR \fB\%ig\fR; input (\fB\%so\fR \fB\%nx\fR); \fB\%ex\fR \fB\%ab\fR \fB\%tm\fR \fB\%tm1\fR \fB\%tmc\fR; traps on input lines and at the end (\fB\%it\fR \fB\%itc\fR \fB\%em\fR), plus \fB\%blm\fR \fB\%lsm\fR; diversions (\fB\%di\fR \fB\%da\fR \fB\%box\fR \fB\%boxa\fR); environments (\fB\%ev\fR \fB\%evc\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCharacter requests:\fR \fB\%cc\fR \fB\%c2\fR \fB\%ec\fR \fB\%eo\fR \fB\%ecs\fR \fB\%ecr\fR \fB\%tr\fR \fB\%trin\fR \fB\%trnt\fR \fB\%char\fR \fB\%fchar\fR \fB\%fschar\fR \fB\%schar\fR \fB\%rchar\fR \fB\%rfschar\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFonts and colors:\fR \fB\%ft\fR \fB\%fp\fR \fB\%ftr\fR \fB\%ul\fR \fB\%cu\fR \fB\%gcolor\fR \fB\%fcolor\fR \fB\%defcolor\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFilling and spacing:\fR \fB\%br\fR \fB\%brp\fR \fB\%fi\fR \fB\%nf\fR \fB\%ad\fR \fB\%na\fR \fB\%ce\fR \fB\%rj\fR \fB\%sp\fR \fB\%bp\fR \fB\%ns\fR \fB\%rs\fR \fB\%in\fR \fB\%ti\fR \fB\%ll\fR \fB\%lt\fR \fB\%ta\fR \fB\%tl\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEscapes:\fR all of them, including \fB\%\e*\fR, \fB\%\en\fR (with auto\-increment), \fB\%\e$\fR, \fB\%\eg\fR, \fB\%\ew\fR, \fB\%\eB\fR, \fB\%\eA\fR, \fB\%\eR\fR, \fB\%\ef\fR, \fB\%\em\fR, \fB\%\eM\fR, \fB\%\eh\fR, \fB\%\el\fR, \fB\%\e(xx\fR, \fB\%\e[name]\fR (groff names, \fB\%uXXXX\fR, accented letters), \fB\%\eC\fR, \fB\%\eN\fR, \fB\%\ec\fR, \fB\%\ep\fR, \fB\%\eZ\fR, \fB\%\eo\fR and \fB\%\eb\fR.
.PP
Some requests are accepted but do nothing, because they are pointless on a reflowing terminal view: page geometry and page traps (\fB\%pl\fR \fB\%po\fR \fB\%pn\fR \fB\%wh\fR \fB\%ch\fR \fB\%dt\fR \fB\%vpt\fR \fB\%mk\fR \fB\%rt\fR \fB\%ne\fR \fB\%os\fR \fB\%sv\fR), sizes and spacing (\fB\%ps\fR \fB\%vs\fR \fB\%ls\fR \fB\%ss\fR \fB\%cs\fR \fB\%bd\fR \fB\%sizes\fR \fB\%fzoom\fR), hyphenation (\fB\%hy\fR \fB\%nh\fR \fB\%hc\fR \fB\%hw\fR \fB\%hla\fR \fB\%hlm\fR \fB\%hpf*\fR \fB\%hym\fR \fB\%hys\fR \fB\%shc\fR \fB\%hcode\fR), kerning and ligatures, line numbering and margin characters (\fB\%nm\fR \fB\%nn\fR \fB\%mc\fR), device and debugging output (\fB\%device\fR \fB\%devicem\fR \fB\%output\fR \fB\%pm\fR \fB\%pnr\fR \fB\%ptr\fR \fB\%pev\fR \fB\%pline\fR \fB\%pvs\fR \fB\%backtrace\fR), warnings, \fB\%fam\fR \fB\%fc\fR \fB\%lc\fR \fB\%tc\fR \fB\%uf\fR \fB\%linetabs\fR, and macro package loading (\fB\%mso\fR \fB\%msoh\fR, since the packages are built in).
.PP
The unsafe requests run only with \fB\%roff.unsafe \%= \%true\fR (\fB\%Options#unsafe\fR). Otherwise they are accepted and ignored:
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBRequest\fR
T}	T{
\fBWith \fB\%unsafe\fB\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%sy \%cmd\fR
T}	T{
runs \fB\%/bin/sh \%\-c \%cmd\fR; the raw wait status goes to register \fB\%systat\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%pso \%cmd\fR
T}	T{
runs the command and reads its output as input
T}
T{
\fB\%pi \%cmd\fR
T}	T{
after parsing, pipes the page formatted as text at 78 columns into the command
T}
T{
\fB\%open \%s \%file\fR / \fB\%opena \%s \%file\fR
T}	T{
opens stream \fB\%s\fR for writing / appending
T}
T{
\fB\%write \%s \%text\fR / \fB\%writec \%s \%text\fR
T}	T{
writes text (copy mode, leading \fB\%"\fR removed) with / without a newline
T}
T{
\fB\%writem \%s \%macro\fR
T}	T{
writes the macro body uninterpreted
T}
T{
\fB\%close \%s\fR
T}	T{
closes the stream (all streams close at the end of parsing)
T}
T{
\fB\%cf \%file\fR / \fB\%trf \%file\fR
T}	T{
sets the file\(aqs lines unprocessed as unfilled text, dropping control characters other than tab
T}
T{
\fB\%rd \%[prompt]\fR
T}	T{
prints the prompt (or a bell) on standard error, then reads input lines from \fB\%Options#stdin\fR up to an empty line
T}
T{
\fB\%\eV[name]\fR
T}	T{
interpolates the environment variable
T}
.TE
.PP
Commands run with standard input and output on the null device, so they never draw over the viewer; \fB\%pso\fR captures the output. The CLI gives \fB\%.rd\fR the terminal only for the page named on the command line, before the viewer starts.
.PP
Lines are left\-aligned (ragged right) and never hyphenated. \fB\%.ad \%b\fR is treated as left; \fB\%.ad \%c\fR and \fB\%.ad \%r\fR work, as do \fB\%.ce\fR and \fB\%.rj\fR.
.SH
DEVELOPMENT
.PP
.TS
tab(	);
l lx.
T{
\fBTarget\fR
T}	T{
\fBDoes\fR
T}
_
T{
\fB\%make \%spec\fR
T}	T{
spec suite
T}
T{
\fB\%make \%build\fR
T}	T{
debug \fB\%bin/docv\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%make \%release\fR
T}	T{
release \fB\%bin/docv\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%make \%docs\fR
T}	T{
API documentation in \fB\%docs/\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%make \%format\fR
T}	T{
\fB\%crystal \%tool \%format\fR
T}
T{
\fB\%make \%install\fR
T}	T{
release build into \fB\%\(ti/.local/bin\fR, man pages into \fB\%\(ti/.local/share/man\fR
T}
.TE
.SH "TYPES"
.TP
.BR "Docv" (3cr)
src/docv/crystal_pages/pages.cr
.TP
.BR "Docv::Align" (3cr)
Horizontal placement of a block\(aqs lines.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Attr" (3cr)
Text attributes of a rendition.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Block" (3cr)
A layout unit.
.TP
.BR "Docv::BlockKind" (3cr)
What a block holds.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Cell" (3cr)
One grid cell: a grapheme with its rendition.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CLI" (3cr)
The \fB\%docv\fR command: shows a manual page or a Markdown document in the viewer, or prints it as text when standard output is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Color" (3cr)
A terminal color: the default color, an entry of the terminal\(aqs 256\-color palette (0\-15 are the ANSI colors of the terminal theme) or a 24\-bit RGB value, packed into 32 bits.
.TP
.BR "Docv::ColorDepth" (3cr)
How many colors the terminal shows.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Colors" (3cr)
Named roff colors: the eight ANSI colors and \fB\%default\fR, plus the colors a page defines with \fB\%.defcolor\fR as 24\-bit values (the screen maps them to fewer colors when the terminal shows fewer).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Config" (3cr)
The user configuration in \fB\%$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini\fR (\fB\%\(ti/.config/docv/config.ini\fR when the variable is unset or not an absolute path).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Config::Error" (3cr)
A configuration file that cannot be parsed or holds an invalid value.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Corpus" (3cr)
The plain text of many pages, for finding text across all of them: each page laid out at \fB\%WIDTH\fR columns (wrapped, without header and footer), one line per line with text, its blanks at either end stripped.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Corpus::Source" (3cr)
A page: its file and modification time in nanoseconds since the epoch (\fB\%Index::Entry#mtime\fR).
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages" (3cr)
Man pages for a Crystal shard (\fB\%docv \%gen\-cr\fR): \fB\%README.md\fR and the API doc comments, read through \fB\%crystal \%docs \%\-\-format \%json\fR, rendered as man(7) roff.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Arg" (3cr)
Method or macro parameter; only its external name matters, to recognize generated members.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Constant" (3cr)
Constant or enum member.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Definition" (3cr)
Definition node of a member: the declared return type and the body.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::DocTool" (3cr)
Runs the compiler\(aqs doc tool.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Error" (3cr)
Raised for every failure reported to the user.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Generator" (3cr)
Writes pages into an output directory.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Inline" (3cr)
Renders the inline content of a markd node as roff: code spans, emphasis, links, images and line breaks.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Literal" (3cr)
Lays out constant values for display.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Location" (3cr)
Source location of a documented type.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Member" (3cr)
Constructor, method or macro.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Page" (3cr)
One generated page; the date is set when it is written.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Pages" (3cr)
Builds every page of a shard: the overview and one page per documented type.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Project" (3cr)
Root of the \fB\%crystal \%docs \%\-\-format \%json\fR output.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Renderer" (3cr)
Writes markd blocks as roff.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Roff" (3cr)
roff escaping for man(7) output.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Shard" (3cr)
The shard being documented: its root, name, version, and the \fB\%require\fR that loads each source file.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::TypeDoc" (3cr)
A documented type; the program, the top level namespace, is one too.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::TypeRef" (3cr)
Reference to another type.
.TP
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages::Types" (3cr)
Lookup tables over the documented types.
.TP
.BR "Docv::DockStyle" (3cr)
How the viewer\(aqs dock sits beside the page: \fB\%Regular\fR narrows the page to make room, \fB\%Overlay\fR draws over the page\(aqs left edge.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Document" (3cr)
A parsed manual page or Markdown document.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Format" (3cr)
What a document was written in: roff with its macro package, or Markdown.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Fuzzy" (3cr)
Fuzzy matching of a query against text, scored like fzf.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Fuzzy::Kind" (3cr)
Character classes that decide bonuses.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Index" (3cr)
Every page along a \fB\%Manpath\fR with the description from its NAME section, and the Markdown documents of its project (\fB\%Manpath#project\fR) with their first heading and paragraph.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Index::Entry" (3cr)
A page file, or a document of the project: its \fIname\fR is the path from the project root and its \fIsection\fR is empty.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout" (3cr)
Turns a \fB\%Document\fR into lines of cells for a given width.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout::Line" (3cr)
One output line.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout::Link" (3cr)
A link on a line: a span link of the document (\fB\%Span#link\fR), or a cross\-reference (\fB\%name(section)\fR) found in the text.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout::Piece" (3cr)
A word, a run of blanks or a tab, ready to be placed.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout::Piece::Kind" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout::Row" (3cr)
A line under construction.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Layout::TableLayout" (3cr)
Renders a \fB\%Table\fR into rows: column widths from content and \fB\%w()\fR minimums, text blocks filled to fit the width when wrapping, an \fB\%expand\fR table widened to the full width, rules and frames drawn with box\-drawing characters.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros" (3cr)
src/docv/macros/mdoc_data.cr
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros::Man" (3cr)
The man(7) macro package (groff an.tmac and an\-ext.tmac), implemented natively on the roff engine.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros::Mdoc" (3cr)
The mdoc(7) semantic macro package, implemented natively on the roff engine.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros::Mdoc::Display" (3cr)
An open \fB\%.Bd\fR display.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros::Mdoc::List" (3cr)
An open \fB\%.Bl\fR list.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros::Mdoc::Token" (3cr)
An argument of a macro line; quoted arguments are never macro names or delimiters.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Macros::MdocData" (3cr)
Static tables of the mdoc(7) package.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Manpath" (3cr)
The manual search path, and lookup of pages along it.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Manpath::ManDb" (3cr)
The \fB\%MANPATH_MAP\fR and \fB\%MANDATORY_MANPATH\fR lines of a man\-db configuration.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Manpath::Project" (3cr)
The project around a directory: its \fIroot\fR, its man page directories (\fIpages\fR) and its Markdown documents (\fIdocuments\fR), in search order.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Manpath::Root" (3cr)
A directory of pages: a tree of \fB\%man<section>\fR directories, or \fIflat\fR with the pages in it; \fIproject\fR when it belongs to the project.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Markdown" (3cr)
Markdown documents: CommonMark with the GitHub extensions (tables, task lists, strikethrough, autolinks and alerts), parsed by markd into the same \fB\%Document\fR model as manual pages.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Markup" (3cr)
What page text is beyond its rendition.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Options" (3cr)
Parsing options.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Palette" (3cr)
The colors of the terminal theme as RGB: the default foreground and background and the 256\-color palette.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Palette::RGB" (3cr)
A 24\-bit color value.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff" (3cr)
src/docv/roff/unsafe.cr
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Builder" (3cr)
Collects formatted output into \fB\%Block\fRs.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Chars" (3cr)
groff special character names (\fB\%\e(xx\fR, \fB\%\e[name]\fR, \fB\%\eC\(aqname\(aq\fR) and their UTF\-8 renderings.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Cursor" (3cr)
A character reader passed by reference between scanning helpers.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Engine" (3cr)
The roff interpreter: input stack, requests, strings, macros, registers, conditionals, escapes.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Env" (3cr)
A formatting environment (\fB\%.ev\fR): the state that shapes output text.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Font" (3cr)
The four terminal fonts; other font names map onto these.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Frame" (3cr)
An input source on the input stack.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Frame::Kind" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Inline" (3cr)
The inline formatter: turns escapes into characters, font and color changes, motions and continuation.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Numeric" (3cr)
roff numeric expressions in basic units, as on a terminal device: one character cell is 24 units wide, one line (\fB\%v\fR) is 40 units high.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Package" (3cr)
A macro package implemented natively (man, mdoc).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Registers" (3cr)
User number registers (\fB\%.nr\fR, \fB\%.af\fR, \fB\%.rr\fR, \fB\%.rnn\fR, \fB\%.aln\fR).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Registers::Register" (3cr)
A register: value, auto\-increment and output format.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Tbl" (3cr)
The tbl(1) preprocessor: reads a \fB\%.TS\fR ...
.TP
.BR "Docv::Roff::Tbl::Spec" (3cr)
The layout of one cell from a format row.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Screen" (3cr)
A cell grid with a front buffer (what the terminal shows) and a back buffer (the next frame).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Source" (3cr)
Reads page files (plain or gzip) and resolves \fB\%.so\fR and \fB\%.nx\fR includes against the page\(aqs manual tree.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Span" (3cr)
A run of text in one rendition.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Style" (3cr)
A text rendition: attributes plus foreground and background color, and the markup of the text (not written to the terminal).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Styles" (3cr)
Interns \fB\%Style\fR values into 16\-bit ids so cells stay small.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Syntax" (3cr)
Syntax highlighting of code blocks through tree\-sitter: a grammar (a shared library) and its \fB\%highlights.scm\fR query, both found where editors and tree\-sitter install them (nvim, helix, \fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/tree\-sitter\fR) or in docv\(aqs own data directory.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Syntax::QueryDirectory" (3cr)
A directory of \fB\%<language>/highlights.scm\fR queries; \fIfirst_wins\fR when its queries give the earlier of two patterns of the same node priority.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table" (3cr)
A tbl(1) table.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table::Cell" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table::CellAlign" (3cr)
Cell alignment from the tbl format keys.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table::CellKind" (3cr)
What a cell holds.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table::Frame" (3cr)
The outer frame.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table::Row" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Table::RowKind" (3cr)
What a row holds.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Tabs" (3cr)
Tab stops in columns, relative to the block\(aqs indent.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Target" (3cr)
Where a link leads.
.TP
.BR "Docv::TargetKind" (3cr)
What a link leads to.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term" (3cr)
src/docv/term/input.cr
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::CellSizeReport" (3cr)
Cell size in pixels (\fB\%CSI \%6 \%; \%h \%; \%w \%t\fR).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Click" (3cr)
Press and release of one button in place; \fB\%count\fR 1\-3 for single to triple clicks.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::ColorSchemeEvent" (3cr)
Dark or light color scheme.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::ColorsReport" (3cr)
Terminal colors in answer to an OSC 21 query: key (\fB\%foreground\fR, \fB\%background\fR, a palette index) to value (\fB\%rgb:rr/gg/bb\fR, empty when unset), as the terminal sent them.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Decoder" (3cr)
Decodes terminal input bytes into raw events: kitty \fB\%CSI \%u\fR keys and their legacy letter/tilde forms, plain UTF\-8 and control bytes, SGR mouse reports, terminal notifications and OSC 21 color reports.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Derived" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Drag" (3cr)
A drag gesture bracketed into start, moves and end.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::DragPhase" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Event" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::FocusEvent" (3cr)
Focus gained or lost.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Input" (3cr)
Turns raw events into the derived events a viewer consumes: the key pressed\-set, text\-versus\-command classification, clicks and multi\-clicks, drag lifecycle, scroll accumulation and pointer enter, move and leave.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Input::Held" (3cr)
A key in the pressed\-set.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Key" (3cr)
Kitty keyboard protocol key numbers for keys that are not text.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::KeyAction" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::KeyboardFlagsReport" (3cr)
Current kitty keyboard flags (\fB\%CSI \%? \%flags \%u\fR).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::KeyCommand" (3cr)
A key command: any other key press or repeat.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::KeyEvent" (3cr)
A key report: key number (un\-shifted codepoint or \fB\%Key\fR constant), the shifted and base\-layout alternates, modifiers, action and text.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::ModeReport" (3cr)
DECRQM answer: \fB\%value\fR 1 set, 2 reset, 0 unknown.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Mods" (3cr)
Modifier state; the wire value is \fB\%1 \%+\fR these bits.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::MouseAction" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::MouseButton" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::MouseEvent" (3cr)
A mouse report in raw coordinates: pixels under SGR\-pixel mode (1016), 1\-based cells under plain SGR (1006).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::MousePress" (3cr)
A mouse button went down, in cell coordinates.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::PointerEnter" (3cr)
The pointer entered or left the window.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::PointerLeave" (3cr)
\&
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::PointerMove" (3cr)
The pointer moved with no button held.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::ResizeEvent" (3cr)
In\-band resize (\fB\%CSI \%48 \%; \%h \%; \%w \%; \%hpx \%; \%wpx \%t\fR).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Scroll" (3cr)
Coalesced wheel reports: positive \fB\%dy\fR scrolls down, positive \fB\%dx\fR right.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Sequences" (3cr)
Escape sequences the viewer writes.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::TextInput" (3cr)
Text input: a key that produced text with no command modifier.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::Tty" (3cr)
The controlling terminal: raw mode, size, and entering/leaving the full\-screen state with all input reporting.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Term::VisibilityEvent" (3cr)
Window restored or minimized.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Theme" (3cr)
The viewer\(aqs styles by role.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Theme::Base" (3cr)
What a color refers to.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Theme::Error" (3cr)
A spec that cannot be parsed.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Theme::Paint" (3cr)
A color of a spec: its base, the fixed color, and a ramp in percent (toward the foreground when positive, the background when negative).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Theme::Role" (3cr)
What a style is for.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Theme::Spec" (3cr)
A parsed spec.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Unicode" (3cr)
Display width of characters and grapheme clusters, and interning of multi\-codepoint clusters so a \fB\%Cell\fR stays a plain value.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer" (3cr)
A full\-screen terminal viewer for a \fB\%Document\fR: a manual page or a Markdown document.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Action" (3cr)
Everything a key can do in the page view.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Bindings" (3cr)
Page view key bindings (\fB\%DEFAULT_BINDINGS\fR unless given).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::CharClass" (3cr)
What a double click selects a run of: a word or punctuation.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Dock" (3cr)
The dock left of the page: the search field on its first row, then a tree of pages (nested \fB\%Picker\fRs the viewer sets: the current page\(aqs group, or every page during a manual search), with a divider on its right edge that resizes it and joins the lines above and below the content.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Dock::Part" (3cr)
What a screen cell of the dock is.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::DragTarget" (3cr)
What a left\-button drag moves.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Field" (3cr)
The text of the search field: typing appends, \fB\%delete_back\fR removes the last grapheme.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::FieldAction" (3cr)
Everything a key can do while the dock\(aqs search field has the keyboard.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::FieldBindings" (3cr)
Search field key bindings (\fB\%FIELD_BINDINGS\fR unless given).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Focus" (3cr)
What has the keyboard.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Frame" (3cr)
The screen layout: a title row with the name, the page\(aqs heading centered and a close mark, a line under it, the content with one blank column of padding on either side, and the vertical scrollbar in the last column (only its thumb is drawn).
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Frame::Region" (3cr)
Where a screen cell lies.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Help" (3cr)
The help: the keys of the page view, the dock\(aqs search field and its tree as they are bound (\fB\%ACTION_HELP\fR, \fB\%FIELD_HELP\fR, \fB\%TREE_HELP\fR), and the mouse gestures, shown in the page area in place of the page, with \fB\%TITLE\fR as the heading of the title row.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Help::Line" (3cr)
A help line: keys or a gesture and what they do; a section title when \fIheading\fR.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Hover" (3cr)
What lies under the mouse pointer, for its shape.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Keymap" (3cr)
Maps key events to values of \fIT\fR: first by physical key (base layout), then by the reported key, then by the shifted symbol without its shift.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Page" (3cr)
A loaded page.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Picker" (3cr)
A fuzzy\-filtered, ranked list with a selection: the page search, and the ranking behind finding in the page.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Picker::Item" (3cr)
A candidate: the \fIlabel\fR shown and matched first, a secondary \fIdetail\fR, the caller\(aqs \fItarget\fR, the \fIrole\fR the label is drawn in, the \fIgroup\fR it ranks in, and the \fIkey\fR a nested picker groups it by.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline" (3cr)
Items folded into groups by the name prefixes they share, for the page search: \fB\%abrt\-cli\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR under \fB\%abrt\fR, and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-xorg\fR under \fB\%abrt\-dump\fR within it.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline::Node" (3cr)
A row of the outline: a group (\fIitem\fR is \-1) of \fIsize\fR items sharing \fIprefix\fR, or the item \fIitem\fR.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Position" (3cr)
Where the reader was on a page, for back navigation.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::TreeAction" (3cr)
Everything a key can do while the dock\(aqs tree has the keyboard.
.TP
.BR "Docv::Viewer::TreeBindings" (3cr)
Dock tree key bindings (\fB\%TREE_BINDINGS\fR unless given).
.TP
.BR "Docv::ViewerSettings" (3cr)
Viewer settings from \fB\%[viewer]\fR: the \fIdock\fR style, its width in columns (\fIdock_width\fR), whether it is open at start (\fIdock_open\fR), and the threads that read and search the text of all pages (\fIsearch_threads\fR; 0 is one less than the processor count).
